§ `Part 1 -- General`

§§ `Dates the text fixes: made, and in force`

-- src:4 | Made 9th February 2015
@ref Made 9th February 2015 (src:4)
`the date the Regulations were made` MEANS YearMonthDay 2015 2 9

-- src:5 | Coming into force 6th April 2016
-- src:14 | (2) These Regulations come into force on 6th April 2016.
@ref Coming into force 6th April 2016 (src:5); regulation 1(2) (src:14)
`the date the Regulations come into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 2016 4 6

§§ `Regulation 1(3): who the Regulations do not apply to`

-- "Pensionable age" is a borrowed term (these Regulations use it without defining it, and the Acts that fix it are not among
-- the inputs), so the date a person reaches it is taken as a fact.
-- Part 5 applies to everyone, so this gate speaks of "these Regulations" meaning every Part but Part 5.
-- src:15 | (3) These Regulations (except Part 5) do not apply to a person who reaches pensionable age before 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 1(3) (src:15)
GIVEN `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Whether the Regulations apply to a person`
`whether Parts 1 to 4 and 6 to 8 apply to a person who reaches pensionable age on` `the date the person reaches pensionable age` MEANS
    IF   Day `the date the person reaches pensionable age` LESS THAN Day `the date the Regulations come into force`
    THEN `these Regulations do not apply to the person, who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016`
    ELSE `these Regulations apply to the person`

§§ `Regulation 1(4): the definitions`

-- "the 1965 Act" and "the 2014 Act" name statutes that are not among the inputs; "graduated retirement benefit"
-- means a benefit under the 1965 Act and is asked as a fact where a rule needs it. The only definition with
-- structure of its own is "deferral period", which is the noun `Deferral period` in spr-nouns.l4.
-- src:16 | (4) {repealed: In these Regulations, “}{repealed: the 2014 Act}{repealed: ” means the Pensions Act 2014.}
-- src:17 | In these Regulations—
-- src:18 | “the 1965 Act” means the National Insurance Act 1965;
-- src:19 | “the 2014 Act” means the Pensions Act 2014;
-- src:20 | “deferral period” means the period during which a person’s entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred;
-- src:21 | “graduated retirement benefit” means any benefit under section 36 (graduated retirement benefit) or 37 (special provisions as to graduated retirement benefit for widows) of the 1965 Act.

§§ `Regulation 1(5): married to a third person`

-- src:22 | (5) For the purposes of these Regulations (except this paragraph), two people are to be treated as if they are not married to each other in relation to times when either of them is married to a third person.
@ref Regulation 1(5) (src:22)
GIVEN `the two people` IS A `Two people at a time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two people are treated as married to each other` `the two people` MEANS
        `the two people`'s `how they are joined` EQUALS `married to each other`
    AND (NOT `the two people`'s `either of them is married to a third person`)

-- Regulation 1(5) takes away only the marriage; two people who are civil partners of each other stay so.
@ref Regulation 1(5) (src:22)
GIVEN `the two people` IS A `Two people at a time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` `the two people` MEANS
        `the two people are treated as married to each other` `the two people`
    OR  `the two people`'s `how they are joined` EQUALS `civil partners of each other`

§§ `A counting convention the later Parts use: a period of months starting on a day`

-- Not a provision of the text. Several regulations speak of a period of N months "starting on" or "beginning with" a day
-- (regulations 4(2), 6(2)(c)(i), and the inserted regulation 6(7)-(8) of the Schedule). Calendar months are meant, and the
-- named day is the first day (fork F7): the period ends on the day before the same day N months on, or on the last day of that
-- month where there is no such day (a period starting on 30 November ends on 28 February, not on the 27th).
GIVEN `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
      `the first day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` `the number of months` `months starting on` `the first day` MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY (`add months` `the first day` `the number of months`) LESS THAN DATE_DAY `the first day`
    THEN `add months` `the first day` `the number of months`
    ELSE Date (Day (`add months` `the first day` `the number of months`) MINUS 1)

§ `Part 1A -- Full rate of State Pension`

-- src:24 | 1A Full rate of state pension
-- src:25 | The full rate of the state pension for the purposes of section 3(1) of the 2014 Act (full rate of state pension) is £241.30 per week.
@ref Regulation 1A (src:25)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full rate of the state pension, in pounds per week` MEANS 241.30
